        <p>Many applications have been made to the War Office by Vo'unteer corps for leave to change their uniform or adopt a fatigue dress. The Commander-in-Chief has in consequence directed that, pending the adoption of a service dress for the Army (a subject now receiving attention), Volunteer commanding officers shall be informed that it is advisable that changes of uniform shall, as far as possible be postponed. If, however, Volunteer b4ttalions wish to make such changes, appli- cations for !eve to do en must state whether funds are avatable for the purpose, or how it is proposed to meet the icitial outlay, attention being directed to the Volunteer Regulation (613 B) bearing upon tbe subject.</p>
