      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-08-16_WidnesExaminer_art0043" n="art0043">
        <p>Flroparison with the stock exhibited on Thursday, last week. The addition of cattle and agricultural Produce classeshas added to the attractiveness of the llovv and we hope the stimulus which it will give to rupetitors may bring about an improvement in 010 farming stock of the district. The society can certainly claim that it has succeeded in 11:sproving the breed of horses io the district and there is ground for believing that a like result Will be attained in the classes which have been added within recent years to the Society's pro- gramme, This year's show was in every respect a Credit to the district and already the Society has gained a high reputation amongst breeders and agriculturalists. With such an excellent president as Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart, who takes a deep in- terest in the welfare of the Society,there is reason to believe that it will continue its progressive Course:for many years to come.</p>
