        <p>1 WARRINGTON, Death of an Old Corporation Employe. 1 Many of our readers will regret to hear of the death, which took place at midnight, on Monday, at his residence in Clifton-street, Latchford, of Mr William Todd, who was one of the oldest employs ght ago for his in the Corporation Gas Department. The deceased had suffered from a lingering malady for several months, and though specialists were consulted little ahtoepree Peacefully away 37,tearntdaihneedpaassfeodrtni at 11.45 on Monday evening. Mr Todd has been connected with the Gas Department from boyhood, wcoaysere and for many years had charge of the fitting section. By his straightforward conduct he had not only won the esteem of his employers, but those placed under his control found in him one of the most con- siderate of foremen. Deceased was in his 51st 3 ear, and leaves a wife and six sons and one daugh- ter to mourn his loss, for whom much sympathy is felt. The funeral took place at the Cemetery yesterday;</p>
