        <p>District classes.—Blood mara.by registered hackney haying produced a living foal, by or stinted to, a registered hackney In 1901 : 1 and special, A C Sparkes, Altrincham ; 2, the Halewood Stud Company, Halewood; 3, J Makeague, Newton-le-Willows. Foals by a registered Hackney out of a snare by a registered Hackney sire 1. AC Sparkes ;2, A L Goodsoo,Knutsford ; 3, F Hardy, Tyntesfield Ashtog-on-Mersey. Yearling colt, igelding, or filly by a registered hackney out of a mare by a registered hackney sire 1. A L Goodson, Heathfield, Knutsford ; 2 and special. Bxors of John Blackshaw,Hatton, near Weerington ; 3, a Smith, Crenshaw Hall, Bold, near Widnes. Two or three year old gelding or filly by a registered hackney out of a mare by a registered hackney sire: 1 and special, A 0 Sparkes; 2, J Makeague ; 3, Exors of John Biaekshaw. Pony brood mare, not exceeding 14 hands, having produced a living foal by, or stinted to, a registered hackney or registered hackney pooy stallion in '1931,—i, C Bower, Appleton, Cheshire : 2. John Makertgue ; 3 and special, Mrs Margarget Garnett Spring- field Farm, Tarbuck. near Liverpool. Foals by registered hackney or registered hackney pony stallion, out of mares I entered in Class 28: 1. C Bower; 2. Robert Taylor. 28. Farnworth-street, Widnes ; 3, A Smith, Stretton Hall. Warrington. Jumpers—l. J T Heap, Clarence Hotel. Ramsbottom ; 2, F W Grange, Oak House, Farodon, Cheshire ; 3, W Pavel!, 1, Meadow-street, Sheffield ; 4, Harry Reynolds, Station Hotel. Hartford, Cheshire.</p>
        <p>Harness Classes.-Mare or gelding 15 hands and over : 1, Miss Sibs S Ross, Reeditleld, Sale, Cheshire; 2, Tom Mitchell, The Park, Rocleshill, near Bradford ; 3, W H Cropper, 15, Lord Street West, Southport. Mare or gelding under 15 hands and exceeding 14 hands : 1 and silver medal, Hustace Smith Benton House, Neweastle.on Tyne; 2. George Ledson Manor House, Bromborough. Cheshire; 3, Frank J Batchelor, Hopwood, Alvechurch, Worcestershire. Mare or gelding not eacee ling 14 hands 1. W J Tatem, Stasndon, Penylan, Cardiff; 2. la ii Franklin, The Field, Derby. Tradesmen's turnouts, district classes (for two wheels) : 1. W and J Strange, St James-street, Warrington ; 2, William Monks, Bridge-street, Warrington; 3, C Bower; 4, W and J Strange. For 4 wheels : 1. The Warrington Slate Company, Warrington ; 2, Peter Walker and Son, the Brewery, War- rington ; 3, William Monks, Bridge-street. Warrington; 4, The Warrington Slate Company, Warrington. CAT 11,E. District Classes-Pair of dairy cows for tenant farmers 1, Richard Clark, Warburton-park, near Warrington; ,2, Thomas Billington. Newton Bank Farm. Preston Brook. One dairy cow for tenant farmers ; 1, Richard Clarke; 2, John H Newton, Warburton, near Warrington. Helfer born In 1899 (for tenant farmers)': 1 and epeeist, John R Newton; 2, Richard Mercer, Halewood,near Liverpool; 3. Samuel W Gould, Foxley-hall, Lynam, Heifer born In 1910 (for tenant farmers). 1. Sam W Gould ;2, Sam W Gould; 3. Mrs Margaret Garnett. Sprinefield Farm, Tarbook. near Liverpool. Bull, born in or before 1898 1, Thomas Billington, Newton Bank Farm. Preston Brook ; 2, John Highfield, Cogshall Hall, near Northwich. Bull born In 1899: 1, Samuel W Gould; 2. Richard Clarke; 3 John Hlgbfleld. Bull born In 1900 : 1, Richard L Warburton, Hatton near Warrington; 2, R Ireland Blackburne, Hale near Liverpool ; 3, Peter Tickle, Preston Brook. CHEESE. Three cheeses 40Ibs, etch or over : 1, John B Gerrard, Arley Moss, near Northwich ; 2, William Gerrard. A