      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-08-16_WidnesExaminer_art0085" n="art0085">
        <head>FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>Northern Union. Lancashire Senior Competition.</p>
        <p>A meeting of this body took place at the Spread Eagle Hotel, Manchester, on Tuesday. Mr J Walsh (Stockport) occuping the chair. The following permits were granted:—H Ricketts (Slaittiwaite) to play with Stockport, T Mawson (Askam) with St Helens, J Piercy MlTrill (Swansea), J Rutter, E Graham, W liraashaw, and F Gibson (local) to play with Altrincham.</p>
        <p>Mr J Underwood (Wigan) tendered his resignation as a member of the committee, which was accepted, a vote of thanks being accorded him for the services he had rendered since the formation of the Union. Mr Frank Hammersley (Wigan) was elected a member of the committee. The following grounds were selected for county matches:— October 26 —Lancashire v Cheshire (at Broughton). January 11.—Lancashire v Cumnerland (at Barrow- in-Furness).</p>
        <p>After consultation with friends in Dover on Monday Madame Isacescu decided to pcstpone her projected swim across the Channel till next year owing to the unsettled state of the weather. It is not very often that firemen are called upon to deal with outbreaks of fire in their own strongholds. Such was the case, however,just before nine o'clock! on Monday night,when a fire of a somewhat serious nature occurred in a tack rosin on the second floor of the Fire Holborn Station in Theobalds-road.Needless to say, plenty of help was lipeedily forthcoming, and the flames were soon sub 'ued.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-08-16_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
