        <p>Week ending Saturday, August 3rd, 1901 During the week, the following births and death were registered : Warrington Registration District, 48 births, 42 deaths. The excess of hi rtne °vit. deaths Was 6 Tne birth rate was equal to 381 per 1,000. The death-rare from all Causes was equal tu 33.9 per 1,000, against 20.4, the avatar of the previous four weeks, and mrainst 16 o,.th, carresponding period of last year. The death-rata from tha seven coief zymotic diseases was equal to 193 per 1,000, against 2 8, the average rate ot the previous four weeks, and against 4.8 the corresponding period of 1900. The ages of mortality were- -0-1 1-5 5-15 15-25 25-65 65 up. Total 28 6 1 6 1 42 The deaths included-21 from diarrhcea, 4 from tuberculosis 1 from lung disease, 1 from drowniog,l2. from all other causes. The following cases of infectious disease have been reported during the week :—Scarlet Fever 1 case, Enteric 4 eases. Total number of _patients in hospital week ending Saturday, 3rd August, 12. Metenrology.—The mean temperature was 64 Fah.. and therefore 5 deg- lower than preceding week. The maximum temperature 73 F., was recorded on the Ist Inst., and the minimum temperature 56 F., on the 2nd inst. The Rainfall measured '56 inch. The general direc- tion was N W. J. GUEST GORNALL, Medical Officer of Health, (pro-tern.)</p>
